WEBVTT

00:00:05.452 --> 00:00:07.484
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:07.522 --> 00:00:08.378
Sammy!

00:00:09.117 --> 00:00:11.088
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:11.674
Go!

00:00:15.393 --> 00:00:16.601
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:17.208 --> 00:00:18.686
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:25.923
This is dad's book. I think dad
wants us to pick up where he left off.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.876
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:27.891 --> 00:00:30.519
Family business. Do you think
Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:31.645
I can't do this alone.

00:00:32.412 --> 00:00:33.163
I'm driving.

00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:07.416
Man, these are some phat houses, huh?

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:08.923
I'd like to live here.

00:01:09.261 --> 00:01:09.599
Yeah.

00:01:10.162 --> 00:01:11.708
Too bad you can't afford it.

00:01:12.662 --> 00:01:13.837
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:14.512 --> 00:01:16.850
This neighborhood will be
damn expensive when it's done.

00:01:41.628 --> 00:01:42.899
This place is perfect...

00:01:43.475 --> 00:01:43.903
Ow!

00:01:45.097 --> 00:01:46.283
...Except for the mosquitoes.

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:51.100
Aah!

00:01:52.264 --> 00:01:52.744
Dustin?

00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:55.183
Help me, I'm trapped!

00:01:56.135 --> 00:01:57.416
I broke my ankle.

00:01:58.969 --> 00:01:59.991
I'll get a rope!

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:03.537
Oh, damn.

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:21.664
Oh god!

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.749
Travis, help!

00:02:33.911 --> 00:02:34.710
Hang on!

00:02:45.035 --> 00:02:46.513
Travis, help!

00:02:46.973 --> 00:02:48.775
Aah! Aaah!

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.525
It's okay, Dustin. It's okay.

00:02:53.964 --> 00:02:54.517
Dustin?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:56.907
Dustin, I'm here.

00:02:59.182 --> 00:02:59.945
Oh, god.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.603
<i>I got something to say.</i>

00:03:26.221 --> 00:03:26.936
<i>Ow!</i>

00:03:29.452 --> 00:03:30.648
<i>Yeah, you're doing all right.</i>

00:03:30.664 --> 00:03:32.282
<i>Gonna start a fire</i>

00:03:35.558 --> 00:03:37.478
You know, we could get
day jobs once in a while.

00:03:38.342 --> 00:03:39.468
Hunting's our day job,

00:03:39.984 --> 00:03:41.110
And the pay is crap.

00:03:41.357 --> 00:03:42.518
Yeah, but hustling pool,

00:03:43.254 --> 00:03:44.158
Credit-Card scams?

00:03:44.842 --> 00:03:46.513
It's not the most honest
thing in the world, Dean.

00:03:46.743 --> 00:03:47.804
Well, let's see... Honest...

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.506
Fun and easy...

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:51.879
It's no contest.

00:03:52.075 --> 00:03:52.484
Besides,

00:03:53.055 --> 00:03:54.404
We're good at it. It's
what we were raised to do.

00:03:54.473 --> 00:03:57.284
How we were raised was
jacked. Yeah, says you.

00:03:57.717 --> 00:03:59.328
We got a new gig or what? Maybe.

00:03:59.568 --> 00:04:02.203
Oasis Plains, Oklahoma.
Not far from here.

00:04:02.498 --> 00:04:03.856
Gas-Company employee.

00:04:04.626 --> 00:04:06.362
Dustin Burwash,

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.907
Supposedly died from creutzfeldt-Jakob.

00:04:09.244 --> 00:04:09.584
Huh?

00:04:10.229 --> 00:04:12.399
Human mad cow disease. Mad cow?

00:04:13.525 --> 00:04:14.856
Wasn't that on "Oprah"?

00:04:15.402 --> 00:04:16.428
You watch "Oprah"?

00:04:19.713 --> 00:04:22.531
So this guy eats a bad burger.
Why is it our kind of thing?

00:04:23.748 --> 00:04:26.528
Mad cow disease causes
massive brain degeneration.

00:04:26.531 --> 00:04:28.998
It takes months, even years
for the damage to appear,

00:04:29.004 --> 00:04:30.188
But this guy, Dustin,

00:04:30.376 --> 00:04:32.994
Sounds like his brain
disintegrated in about an hour,

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.258
Maybe less.

00:04:34.275 --> 00:04:35.748
Okay, that's weird. Yeah.

00:04:36.217 --> 00:04:37.523
Now, it could be a disease,

00:04:38.184 --> 00:04:39.710
Or it could be something much nastier.

00:04:40.658 --> 00:04:42.301
All right, Oklahoma.

00:04:42.947 --> 00:04:44.429
Man, work, work, work.

00:04:45.339 --> 00:04:46.733
No time to spend my money.

00:04:47.862 --> 00:04:51.770
<i>We got the power, we got the glory</i>

00:04:51.954 --> 00:04:54.020
<i>Just say you need it...</i>

00:05:01.851 --> 00:05:02.802
Travis Weaver?

00:05:04.561 --> 00:05:05.358
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:06.715 --> 00:05:08.756
Are you the Travis who
worked with uncle Dusty?

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.489
Dustin never mentioned nephews.

00:05:12.052 --> 00:05:12.650
Really?

00:05:13.108 --> 00:05:14.316
Well, he sure mentioned you.

00:05:14.363 --> 00:05:15.829
He said you were the greatest.

00:05:16.275 --> 00:05:17.037
Oh, he did?

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:18.182
Huh.

00:05:18.898 --> 00:05:20.681
So, we wanted to ask you...

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.417
What exactly happened out there?

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:24.693
I'm not sure.

00:05:25.168 --> 00:05:27.866
He fell in the sinkhole. I went
to the truck to get some rope, and

00:05:28.382 --> 00:05:29.696
By the time I got back...

00:05:30.412 --> 00:05:31.620
What'd you see?

00:05:33.145 --> 00:05:33.591
Nothing.

00:05:34.313 --> 00:05:35.052
Just Dustin.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.870
No wounds or anything?

00:05:37.316 --> 00:05:38.231
Well, he was bleeding

00:05:38.442 --> 00:05:40.846
From his eyes and his ears, his nose,

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:42.242
That's it.

00:05:42.876 --> 00:05:44.670
So do you think it could
be this whole mad cow thing?

00:05:46.366 --> 00:05:47.035
I don't know.

00:05:47.645 --> 00:05:48.853
That's what the doctors are saying.

00:05:48.923 --> 00:05:49.827
But if it was,

00:05:50.472 --> 00:05:54.824
He would have acted strange beforehand,
like dementia, loss of motor control.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.821
You ever notice anything like that? No.

00:05:57.199 --> 00:05:57.752
No way.

00:05:59.002 --> 00:06:01.316
Yeah, but if it wasn't some
disease, what the hell was it?

00:06:02.517 --> 00:06:03.395
That's a good question.

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:03.972
Yep.

00:06:04.182 --> 00:06:05.595
Can you tell us where this happened?

00:06:06.361 --> 00:06:06.751
Yeah.

00:06:30.568 --> 00:06:31.024
Huh.

00:06:32.575 --> 00:06:33.296
What do you think?

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.002
I don't know,

00:06:35.017 --> 00:06:37.607
But if that guy Travis was right,
it happened pretty damn fast.

00:06:38.389 --> 00:06:39.200
So what?

00:06:39.523 --> 00:06:41.175
Some sort of creature
chewed on his brain?

00:06:41.198 --> 00:06:42.625
No, there'd be an entry wound.

00:06:43.046 --> 00:06:44.744
Sounds like this thing
worked from the inside.

00:06:48.579 --> 00:06:49.105
Huh.

00:06:50.232 --> 00:06:52.088
It looks like there's only room for one.

00:06:52.899 --> 00:06:53.966
You want to flip a coin?

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.240
Dean, we have no idea what's down there.

00:06:58.773 --> 00:07:00.268
All right, I'll go if you're scared.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.551
Scared?

00:07:01.956 --> 00:07:03.068
Flip the damn coin.

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:07.563
Call it in the air...

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:08.405
Chicken.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.034
I'm going.

00:07:11.102 --> 00:07:12.011
I said I'd go.

00:07:12.324 --> 00:07:13.333
I'm going.

00:07:13.752 --> 00:07:14.600
All right.

00:07:16.509 --> 00:07:17.858
Don't drop me.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.107
So, you found some beetles

00:07:24.212 --> 00:07:25.550
In a hole in the ground.

00:07:26.429 --> 00:07:27.860
That's shocking, Sam.

00:07:28.388 --> 00:07:30.429
There were no tunnels, no tracks,

00:07:30.852 --> 00:07:33.385
No evidence of any other
kind of creature down there.

00:07:33.635 --> 00:07:35.386
You know, some beetles do eat meat.

00:07:35.405 --> 00:07:38.192
Now, it's usually dead meat, but...
How many did you find down there?

00:07:38.464 --> 00:07:38.924
10.

00:07:40.365 --> 00:07:42.730
It would take a whole lot more than
that to eat out somebody's brain.

00:07:42.843 --> 00:07:44.063
Well, maybe there were more.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.502
I don't know. It sounds
like a stretch to me.

00:07:46.524 --> 00:07:49.362
We need more information on
the area, the neighborhood,

00:07:49.386 --> 00:07:52.025
Whether something like this
has ever happened before.

00:07:54.007 --> 00:07:54.524
What?

00:07:55.239 --> 00:07:56.588
I know a good place to start.

00:07:58.154 --> 00:08:00.429
I'm kind of hungry for a
little barbecue, how about you?

00:08:03.045 --> 00:08:04.652
What, we can't talk to the locals?

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.874
And the free food's got nothing to do
with it? Of course not. I'm a professional.

00:08:08.456 --> 00:08:08.953
Right.

00:08:28.913 --> 00:08:31.491
Growing up in a place like
this would freak me out.

00:08:32.157 --> 00:08:32.795
Why?

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.362
The manicured lawns, the"how
was your day, honey?"...

00:08:37.462 --> 00:08:38.940
I'd blow my brains out.

00:08:40.395 --> 00:08:42.213
There's nothing wrong with normal.

00:08:43.445 --> 00:08:45.380
I'd take our family over normal any day.

00:08:49.598 --> 00:08:51.440
Welcome. Is this the barbecue?

00:08:51.534 --> 00:08:53.774
Yeah, not the best weather, but...

00:08:53.962 --> 00:08:57.704
I'm Larry Pike, the developer here,
and you are? Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:57.968 --> 00:08:59.563
Sam, Dean, good to meet you.

00:08:59.974 --> 00:09:02.578
So, you two are interested
in Oasis Plains? Yes, sir.

00:09:03.106 --> 00:09:03.962
Let me just say

00:09:04.068 --> 00:09:07.552
That we accept homeowners of
any race,religion, color, or...

00:09:08.122 --> 00:09:09.448
Sexual orientation.

00:09:11.078 --> 00:09:12.099
We're brothers.

00:09:12.881 --> 00:09:16.729
Our father is getting on in years, and
we're just looking for a place for him.

00:09:16.823 --> 00:09:17.409
Great,

00:09:17.597 --> 00:09:19.720
Great. Well, seniors are
welcome, too. Come on in.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.889
You said you were the developer?

00:09:26.088 --> 00:09:28.975
18 months ago, I was walking
this valley with my survey team.

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:32.098
There was nothing here but
scrub brush and squirrels,

00:09:32.296 --> 00:09:34.914
And you know what? We built
such a nice place to live

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.607
That I actually bought into
it myself. This is our house.

00:09:37.776 --> 00:09:42.012
We're the first family in Oasis
Plains. This is my wife, Joanie.

00:09:42.088 --> 00:09:42.951
Hi, there. Hi,

00:09:42.998 --> 00:09:44.556
Nice to meet you. Sam and Dean.

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:46.031
Sam. Joannie.

00:09:46.087 --> 00:09:47.814
Tell them how much you
love the place, honey.

00:09:48.217 --> 00:09:51.141
And lie if you have to because
I need to sell some houses.

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:53.694
Boys, if you'll excuse me.

00:09:54.548 --> 00:09:58.104
Don't let his salesman routine scare
you. This really is a great place to live.

00:09:58.246 --> 00:10:00.132
Hi, I'm Linda Bloom, head of sales.

00:10:00.226 --> 00:10:01.868
And Linda was second to move in.

00:10:01.981 --> 00:10:03.764
She's a very noisy neighbor, though.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.835
She's kidding, of course.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.716
I take it you two are interested
in becoming homeowners.

00:10:10.421 --> 00:10:11.650
Well... Y-Yeah.

00:10:11.653 --> 00:10:16.859
Well, let me just say that we accept
homeowners of any race, religion, color,or...

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.252
Sexual orientation.

00:10:19.615 --> 00:10:20.108
Hmm.

00:10:20.272 --> 00:10:20.976
Right.

00:10:21.351 --> 00:10:23.463
Uh, I'm gonna go talk to Larry.

00:10:23.791 --> 00:10:24.659
Okay, honey?

00:10:30.317 --> 00:10:31.877
You have three choices...

00:10:31.995 --> 00:10:34.047
Carpet, hardwood, and tile.

00:10:34.118 --> 00:10:34.845
Whoa,

00:10:35.514 --> 00:10:36.886
Someone likes bugs.

00:10:37.508 --> 00:10:40.523
My son. He's into insects.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.758
He's very inquisitive.

00:10:43.509 --> 00:10:44.130
Hmm.

00:10:44.283 --> 00:10:47.509
Who can say no to a steam
shower? I use mine every day.

00:10:47.919 --> 00:10:48.940
Sounds great.

00:10:49.075 --> 00:10:52.336
You also have three different
whirlpool tubs to choose from.

00:10:52.343 --> 00:10:54.522
The hardware for the tubs
include nickel, brass,

00:10:54.574 --> 00:10:57.557
And when you see the kitchens,
you can choose from... Excuse me.

00:10:57.602 --> 00:10:59.021
Um, okay.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:12.371
Is this yours?

00:11:12.694 --> 00:11:14.351
You gonna tell my dad? I don't know.

00:11:14.541 --> 00:11:15.483
Who's your dad?

00:11:16.188 --> 00:11:16.873
Yeah.

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:19.610
Larry usually skips me in
the family introductions.

00:11:19.715 --> 00:11:23.281
Ouch. First-Name basis with the
old man... sounds pretty grim.

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:25.252
Well, I'm not exactly brochure material.

00:11:25.572 --> 00:11:27.924
Well, hang in there. It gets
better. Alright? I promise.

00:11:28.458 --> 00:11:29.068
When?

00:11:29.091 --> 00:11:29.713
Matthew!

00:11:38.869 --> 00:11:41.215
I am so sorry about my son and his...

00:11:41.344 --> 00:11:42.834
Pet. It's no bother.

00:11:43.338 --> 00:11:44.394
Excuse us.

00:11:51.612 --> 00:11:52.785
Remind you of somebody?

00:11:57.536 --> 00:11:58.169
Dad?

00:11:59.654 --> 00:12:00.980
Dad never treated us like that.

00:12:01.766 --> 00:12:03.854
Well, dad never treated you
like that. You were perfect.

00:12:03.865 --> 00:12:05.343
He was all over my case.

00:12:07.098 --> 00:12:08.283
You don't remember?

00:12:09.162 --> 00:12:11.555
Maybe he had to raise his voice,
but sometimes you were out of line.

00:12:11.572 --> 00:12:12.294
Right.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:16.177
Right, like when I said I'd rather
play soccer than learn bow hunting.

00:12:16.371 --> 00:12:17.920
Bow hunting's an important skill.

00:12:19.057 --> 00:12:19.796
Whatever.

00:12:21.181 --> 00:12:22.917
How was your tour?

00:12:23.104 --> 00:12:25.110
It was excellent.I'm ready to buy.

00:12:25.305 --> 00:12:27.112
So you might be onto something.

00:12:27.745 --> 00:12:30.443
Looks like Dustin Burwash wasn't
the first strange death around here.

00:12:30.607 --> 00:12:31.205
What happened?

00:12:31.362 --> 00:12:33.212
About a year ago,
before they broke ground,

00:12:33.272 --> 00:12:35.511
One of Larry's surveyors
dropped dead while on the job.

00:12:35.859 --> 00:12:38.436
Get this... severe allergic
reaction to bee stings.

00:12:38.752 --> 00:12:39.984
More bugs. More bugs.

00:12:42.547 --> 00:12:44.912
I've heard of killer
bees, but killer beetles?

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.996
What is it that could
make different bugs attack?

00:12:48.761 --> 00:12:51.683
Well, hauntings sometimes
include bug manifestations.

00:12:51.718 --> 00:12:54.199
Yeah, but I didn't see any
evidence of ghost activity.

00:12:54.349 --> 00:12:55.449
Yeah, me neither.

00:12:57.247 --> 00:13:00.394
Maybe they're being controlled
somehow... by something or someone.

00:13:00.929 --> 00:13:02.172
You mean like "Willard"?

00:13:02.206 --> 00:13:03.792
Yeah, bugs instead of rats.

00:13:05.316 --> 00:13:10.844
There are cases of psychic connections between
people and animals, elementals, telepaths.

00:13:10.856 --> 00:13:12.944
Yeah, that whole Timmy/Lassie thing.

00:13:14.254 --> 00:13:15.532
Larry's kid...

00:13:16.107 --> 00:13:17.362
Bugs for pets.

00:13:17.831 --> 00:13:18.981
Matt? Yeah.

00:13:20.784 --> 00:13:24.186
He did try to scare the realtor with
a tarantula. Think he's our willard?

00:13:24.373 --> 00:13:25.288
I don't know.

00:13:25.347 --> 00:13:26.989
Anything's possible, I guess.

00:13:29.167 --> 00:13:31.055
Ooh, hey, pull over here.

00:13:39.918 --> 00:13:41.314
What are we doing here?

00:13:45.185 --> 00:13:46.768
It's too late to talk to anybody else.

00:13:48.701 --> 00:13:51.117
We're gonna squat in an empty house?

00:13:51.739 --> 00:13:53.693
I want to try the steam shower. Come on.

00:13:54.608 --> 00:13:55.476
Come on!

00:14:23.133 --> 00:14:26.440
Atoko valley county began
mandatory insecticide

00:14:26.478 --> 00:14:29.209
Spraying across a wide
swath of the district today.

00:14:29.249 --> 00:14:34.982
Authorities say the decision to spray was made
because of several recent cases of west nile virus,

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.489
Coupled with a dramatic increase in
the mosquito population in some areas.

00:14:39.809 --> 00:14:44.292
Although some residents cite concerns about
the high levels of pesticide being used...

00:15:09.525 --> 00:15:12.763
Aaah! Aaah!

00:15:42.331 --> 00:15:43.570
You ever coming out of there?

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:44.640
What?!

00:15:44.912 --> 00:15:47.887
Dean, a police call came
in on the scanner. Hold on.

00:15:47.929 --> 00:15:50.800
Someone was found dead three
blocks from here. Come on.

00:15:53.364 --> 00:15:54.838
This shower is awesome.

00:15:55.072 --> 00:15:55.948
Come on.

00:16:24.188 --> 00:16:26.328
Okay, look, I don't know
anything more right now.

00:16:26.375 --> 00:16:27.989
I'll have to call you back.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:28.843
All right.

00:16:30.251 --> 00:16:31.978
Hello, you're back early.

00:16:31.996 --> 00:16:35.609
Yeah, we wanted to take another look
at the neighborhood. What's going on?

00:16:37.855 --> 00:16:41.308
You guys met Linda
Bloom at the barbecue?

00:16:41.486 --> 00:16:42.322
The realtor.

00:16:42.903 --> 00:16:43.936
Well, she, uh,

00:16:44.831 --> 00:16:46.041
Passed away last night.

00:16:47.496 --> 00:16:48.190
What happened?

00:16:49.553 --> 00:16:50.839
I'm still trying to find out.

00:16:51.402 --> 00:16:53.204
I identified the body for the police.

00:16:54.733 --> 00:16:56.460
I'm sorry. This isn't a good time.

00:16:56.724 --> 00:16:57.325
It's okay.

00:16:57.484 --> 00:16:58.357
Excuse me.

00:17:01.747 --> 00:17:03.052
You know what we have to do, right?

00:17:04.196 --> 00:17:06.786
We got to get in that house.
See if we got a bug problem.

00:17:34.382 --> 00:17:35.902
This looks like the place.

00:17:49.576 --> 00:17:50.468
Spiders.

00:17:51.189 --> 00:17:52.374
From spider boy?

00:17:52.562 --> 00:17:53.312
Matt.

00:17:55.119 --> 00:17:55.905
Maybe.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.633
Isn't his house that way?

00:18:20.692 --> 00:18:21.642
Yep.

00:18:25.149 --> 00:18:26.663
So where's he going?

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:53.545
Hey, Matt.

00:18:54.355 --> 00:18:55.364
Remember me?

00:18:56.321 --> 00:18:57.294
What are you doing out here?

00:18:57.412 --> 00:18:58.784
We want to talk to you.

00:19:00.368 --> 00:19:01.916
You're not here to buy a house, are you?

00:19:02.956 --> 00:19:03.718
Wait,

00:19:04.539 --> 00:19:05.830
You're not serial killers?

00:19:06.182 --> 00:19:08.281
No, no. No, I think you're safe.

00:19:09.618 --> 00:19:10.651
So, Matt...

00:19:11.798 --> 00:19:13.639
You sure know a lot about insects.

00:19:14.765 --> 00:19:15.340
So?

00:19:16.534 --> 00:19:18.681
Did you hear what happened
to Linda, the realtor?

00:19:20.499 --> 00:19:21.871
I hear she died this morning.

00:19:22.054 --> 00:19:23.133
Mm, that's right.

00:19:23.497 --> 00:19:24.740
Spider bites.

00:19:25.608 --> 00:19:26.359
Matt,

00:19:27.227 --> 00:19:29.526
You tried to scare her with a spider.

00:19:31.153 --> 00:19:31.751
Wait,

00:19:32.443 --> 00:19:33.874
You think I had
something to do with that?

00:19:34.461 --> 00:19:35.528
You tell us.

00:19:36.326 --> 00:19:38.320
That tarantula was a joke.

00:19:38.918 --> 00:19:42.408
Anyway, that wouldn't explain the
bee attack or the gas-Company guy.

00:19:43.768 --> 00:19:45.071
You know about those?

00:19:45.505 --> 00:19:46.877
There is something going on here.

00:19:47.346 --> 00:19:48.437
I don't know what,

00:19:48.539 --> 00:19:49.020
But

00:19:49.443 --> 00:19:51.261
Something's happening with the insects.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.008
Let me show you something.

00:20:00.856 --> 00:20:03.858
So, if you knew about all this
bug stuff, why not tell your dad?

00:20:03.964 --> 00:20:05.794
Maybe he could clear everybody out.

00:20:05.958 --> 00:20:07.671
Believe me, I've tried, but

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.701
Larry doesn't listen to me.

00:20:09.947 --> 00:20:10.604
Why not?

00:20:10.956 --> 00:20:11.941
Mostly?

00:20:12.082 --> 00:20:14.065
He's too disappointed in his freak son.

00:20:15.836 --> 00:20:16.751
I hear ya.

00:20:17.428 --> 00:20:18.202
You do?

00:20:20.501 --> 00:20:21.662
Matt, how old are you?

00:20:21.733 --> 00:20:22.530
16.

00:20:23.868 --> 00:20:26.624
Well, don't sweat it 'cause in two
years something great's gonna happen.

00:20:27.304 --> 00:20:28.617
What? College.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:31.714
You'll be able to get out of
that house and away from your dad.

00:20:32.301 --> 00:20:34.802
What kind of advice is that? A
kid should stick with his family.

00:20:39.928 --> 00:20:40.961
How much further, Matt?

00:20:41.133 --> 00:20:42.141
We're close.

00:21:03.465 --> 00:21:05.671
I've been keeping track of
the insect population. It's

00:21:05.893 --> 00:21:07.653
Part of an A.P. Science class.

00:21:09.002 --> 00:21:10.269
You two are like peas in a pod.

00:21:12.331 --> 00:21:13.257
What's been happening?

00:21:13.492 --> 00:21:14.313
A lot.

00:21:15.005 --> 00:21:17.527
I mean, from bees to earthworms,

00:21:17.957 --> 00:21:19.083
Beetles...

00:21:19.212 --> 00:21:20.690
You name it. It's

00:21:20.748 --> 00:21:22.543
Like they're congregating here.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:23.259
Why?

00:21:23.775 --> 00:21:24.701
I don't know.

00:21:27.326 --> 00:21:28.112
What's that?

00:22:04.937 --> 00:22:06.122
There's something down there.

00:22:12.808 --> 00:22:14.181
Oh, come on.

00:23:04.632 --> 00:23:07.385
So, a bunch of skeletons
in an unmarked grave.

00:23:07.502 --> 00:23:09.473
Yeah, maybe this is a haunting...

00:23:09.602 --> 00:23:10.904
Some pissed-Off spirits,

00:23:11.244 --> 00:23:13.542
Some unfinished business. Yeah, maybe.

00:23:13.624 --> 00:23:15.583
The question is, why bugs

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:16.768
And why now?

00:23:17.225 --> 00:23:18.703
That's two questions.

00:23:20.029 --> 00:23:21.648
So, with that kid back there...

00:23:21.984 --> 00:23:24.471
How could you tell him to just
ditch his family like that?

00:23:24.682 --> 00:23:25.879
Just, uh,

00:23:26.278 --> 00:23:27.943
I know what the kid's going through.

00:23:28.267 --> 00:23:31.751
How about telling him to respect his old
man? How's that for advice? Dean, come on.

00:23:32.455 --> 00:23:34.132
This isn't about his old man.

00:23:34.214 --> 00:23:35.517
You think I didn't respect dad.

00:23:35.634 --> 00:23:36.854
That's what this is about.

00:23:37.998 --> 00:23:39.464
Just forget it. Sorry I brought it up.

00:23:39.523 --> 00:23:40.555
I respected him,

00:23:41.318 --> 00:23:42.702
But no matter what I did,

00:23:42.948 --> 00:23:44.192
It was never good enough.

00:23:44.309 --> 00:23:46.972
What are you saying, that dad
was disappointed in you? Was?

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:49.153
Is...

00:23:49.623 --> 00:23:51.757
Always has been. Why
would you think that?

00:23:51.804 --> 00:23:53.540
Because I didn't want to bow hunt

00:23:53.709 --> 00:23:56.653
Or hustle pool, because I wanted
to go to school and live my life,

00:23:56.668 --> 00:23:59.052
Which in our whacked-Out
family made me the freak.

00:24:01.127 --> 00:24:03.461
Yeah, you were kind of like the
blond chick in "the munsters."

00:24:04.799 --> 00:24:05.444
Dean,

00:24:06.183 --> 00:24:08.728
You know what most dads are when
their kids score a full ride?

00:24:09.702 --> 00:24:10.417
Proud.

00:24:11.919 --> 00:24:14.112
Most dads don't toss their
kids out of the house.

00:24:15.457 --> 00:24:16.712
I remember that fight.

00:24:17.779 --> 00:24:20.536
In fact, I seem to recall a few choice
phrases coming out of your mouth.

00:24:25.339 --> 00:24:26.114
You know,

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:29.316
Truth is, when we finally do find dad,

00:24:30.243 --> 00:24:32.272
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:24:34.055 --> 00:24:36.056
Sam, dad was never disappointed in you.

00:24:37.288 --> 00:24:37.980
Never.

00:24:39.247 --> 00:24:40.432
He was scared.

00:24:41.155 --> 00:24:42.328
What are you talking about?

00:24:42.375 --> 00:24:45.038
He was afraid of what could have
happened to you if he wasn't around.

00:24:46.563 --> 00:24:48.263
But even when you two weren't talking,

00:24:49.104 --> 00:24:51.345
He used to swing by
Stanford whenever he could,

00:24:52.107 --> 00:24:53.057
Keep an eye on you,

00:24:53.796 --> 00:24:55.087
Make sure you were safe.

00:24:55.779 --> 00:24:56.717
What?

00:24:58.133 --> 00:24:58.778
Yeah.

00:25:02.943 --> 00:25:04.585
Why didn't he tell me any of that?

00:25:06.549 --> 00:25:09.118
It's a two-Way street, dude. You
could have picked up the phone.

00:25:14.901 --> 00:25:16.736
Come on, we're gonna be
late for our appointment.

00:25:25.053 --> 00:25:26.566
So, you two are students?

00:25:26.991 --> 00:25:28.058
Yeah.

00:25:28.164 --> 00:25:30.416
Yeah, we're in your class.

00:25:30.663 --> 00:25:31.965
Anthro 101.

00:25:32.363 --> 00:25:33.525
Oh, yeah.

00:25:33.595 --> 00:25:34.369
So,

00:25:34.440 --> 00:25:36.410
What about the bones, Professor?

00:25:37.288 --> 00:25:40.045
This is quite an
interesting find you've made.

00:25:40.092 --> 00:25:44.139
I'd say they're 170
years old, give or take.

00:25:44.725 --> 00:25:46.555
The time frame and the geography

00:25:46.574 --> 00:25:48.498
Heavily suggest native american.

00:25:48.944 --> 00:25:52.281
Were there any tribes or
reservations on that land?

00:25:52.363 --> 00:25:55.061
Not according to the historical record,

00:25:55.132 --> 00:25:56.059
But

00:25:56.493 --> 00:25:57.701
The, uh...

00:25:57.748 --> 00:26:01.889
Relocation of native peoples
was quite common at that time.

00:26:02.135 --> 00:26:02.874
Right.

00:26:03.678 --> 00:26:04.312
Well,

00:26:04.828 --> 00:26:06.364
Are there any local legends,

00:26:06.576 --> 00:26:08.793
Oral histories about the area?

00:26:09.778 --> 00:26:10.963
Well...

00:26:11.573 --> 00:26:15.139
You know, there's a
euchee tribe in Sapulpa.

00:26:15.369 --> 00:26:17.128
It's about 60 miles from here.

00:26:18.536 --> 00:26:20.503
Someone out there might know the truth.

00:26:23.612 --> 00:26:24.644
All right.

00:27:11.038 --> 00:27:12.242
Joe Whitetree?

00:27:13.968 --> 00:27:16.983
We'd like to ask you a few
questions, if that's all right.

00:27:17.587 --> 00:27:19.124
We're students from the university.

00:27:19.182 --> 00:27:21.235
No, you're not. You're lying.

00:27:23.276 --> 00:27:24.074
Um,

00:27:24.672 --> 00:27:27.464
The truth is... You know
who starts sentence with

00:27:27.589 --> 00:27:28.669
"Truth is"?

00:27:29.067 --> 00:27:30.064
Liars.

00:27:34.963 --> 00:27:36.722
Have you heard of Oasis Plains?

00:27:36.769 --> 00:27:39.232
It's a housing development
near the Atoka valley.

00:27:41.948 --> 00:27:42.969
I like him.

00:27:43.661 --> 00:27:44.893
He's not a liar.

00:27:45.984 --> 00:27:47.157
I know the area.

00:27:48.541 --> 00:27:50.535
What can you tell us
about the history there?

00:27:50.672 --> 00:27:51.775
Why do you want to know?

00:27:52.444 --> 00:27:53.687
Something...

00:27:54.086 --> 00:27:55.153
Something bad

00:27:56.021 --> 00:27:57.992
Is happening in Oasis Plains.

00:27:58.959 --> 00:28:02.654
We think it might have something to do
with some old bones we found down there...

00:28:03.863 --> 00:28:05.329
Native american bones.

00:28:10.192 --> 00:28:12.503
I'll tell you what my
grandfather told me,

00:28:13.265 --> 00:28:15.107
What his grandfather told him.

00:28:15.857 --> 00:28:17.335
200 years ago,

00:28:17.602 --> 00:28:20.335
A band of my ancestors
lived in that valley.

00:28:21.086 --> 00:28:24.687
One day, the american
calvary came to relocate them.

00:28:27.770 --> 00:28:29.365
They were resistant...

00:28:29.999 --> 00:28:31.665
Calvary impatient.

00:28:33.248 --> 00:28:35.019
As my grandfather put it,

00:28:36.052 --> 00:28:36.887
On a night,

00:28:37.016 --> 00:28:38.060
The moon

00:28:38.388 --> 00:28:39.350
And the sun

00:28:39.631 --> 00:28:41.872
Shared the sky as equals,

00:28:43.162 --> 00:28:45.848
The calvary first raided our village.

00:28:46.466 --> 00:28:47.499
They murdered,

00:28:48.202 --> 00:28:49.035
Raped.

00:28:50.114 --> 00:28:52.470
The next day, the calvary came again,

00:28:52.752 --> 00:28:54.851
And the next and the next.

00:28:55.250 --> 00:28:58.347
And on the sixth night, the
calvary came one last time,

00:28:59.492 --> 00:29:01.510
And by the time the sun rose,

00:29:01.686 --> 00:29:03.820
Every man, woman, and child

00:29:03.891 --> 00:29:05.624
Still in the village

00:29:05.976 --> 00:29:07.008
Was dead.

00:29:11.625 --> 00:29:13.455
They say on the sixth night,

00:29:13.608 --> 00:29:16.212
As the chief of the village lay dying,

00:29:16.564 --> 00:29:18.440
He whispered to the heavens

00:29:19.285 --> 00:29:22.616
That no white man would
ever tarnish this land again.

00:29:23.536 --> 00:29:24.545
Nature

00:29:24.920 --> 00:29:26.105
Would rise up

00:29:26.773 --> 00:29:28.357
And protect the valley,

00:29:28.521 --> 00:29:31.606
And it would bring as many
days of misery and death

00:29:32.177 --> 00:29:33.326
To the white man

00:29:33.983 --> 00:29:36.106
As the calvary had
brought upon his people.

00:29:37.901 --> 00:29:38.992
Insects.

00:29:39.880 --> 00:29:41.299
That sounds like nature to me.

00:29:42.848 --> 00:29:43.915
Six days?

00:29:44.185 --> 00:29:46.285
And on the night of the sixth day,

00:29:47.183 --> 00:29:48.814
None would survive.

00:29:57.243 --> 00:29:59.155
When did the gas-Company man die?

00:30:00.140 --> 00:30:02.744
Let's see, we got here
tuesday, so friday the 20th.

00:30:03.265 --> 00:30:04.168
March 20th.

00:30:05.118 --> 00:30:06.549
That's the spring equinox.

00:30:07.253 --> 00:30:09.611
The night, the sun and the
moon share the sky as equals.

00:30:09.707 --> 00:30:13.542
So every year about this time,
anybody in Oasis Plains is in danger.

00:30:14.211 --> 00:30:17.796
Larry built his neighborhood on cursed land.
And on the sixth night... that's tonight.

00:30:18.125 --> 00:30:21.550
If we don't do something, Larry's
family will be dead by sunrise.

00:30:22.895 --> 00:30:24.303
So how do we break a curse?

00:30:24.631 --> 00:30:25.769
You don't break a curse.

00:30:26.168 --> 00:30:28.350
You get out of its way. We got
to get those people out now.

00:31:46.564 --> 00:31:49.579
Yes, mr. Pike, there's a main-Line
gas leak in your neighborhood.

00:31:49.661 --> 00:31:51.209
God, really? And how big?

00:31:51.315 --> 00:31:54.060
Well, it's fairly extensive.
I don't want to alarm you, but

00:31:54.189 --> 00:31:58.001
We need your family out of the vicinity for
at least 12 hours or so, just to be safe.

00:31:58.139 --> 00:31:59.148
And who is this again?

00:31:59.207 --> 00:32:01.940
Travis Weaver. I work for
Oklahoma gas and power.

00:32:01.987 --> 00:32:02.561
Uh-Huh.

00:32:02.770 --> 00:32:06.606
The problemis I know Travis. He's worked
with us for a year. So who is this?

00:32:07.134 --> 00:32:08.152
Uh...

00:32:09.842 --> 00:32:10.886
Give me the phone.

00:32:19.876 --> 00:32:20.509
Hello?

00:32:20.626 --> 00:32:21.623
Matt, it's Sam.

00:32:21.905 --> 00:32:23.907
Sam, my backyard's
crawling with cockroaches.

00:32:23.908 --> 00:32:27.356
Matt, just listen. You have to get your
family out of that house right now, okay?

00:32:27.648 --> 00:32:28.502
What, why?

00:32:29.390 --> 00:32:30.639
Because something's coming.

00:32:31.296 --> 00:32:32.132
More bugs.

00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:33.738
Yeah, a lot more.

00:32:34.828 --> 00:32:36.922
My dad doesn't listen in
the best of circumstances.

00:32:36.942 --> 00:32:39.889
What am I supposed to tell him?
You got to make him listen, okay?

00:32:40.088 --> 00:32:41.321
Give me the phone. Give me the phone!

00:32:41.532 --> 00:32:44.679
Matt, under no circumstances are you to
tell the truth. He'll just think you're nuts.

00:32:44.808 --> 00:32:47.332
But he's my... Tell him you have
a sharp pain in your right side,

00:32:47.391 --> 00:32:48.952
And you got to go to the hospital, okay?

00:32:49.083 --> 00:32:50.774
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

00:32:54.625 --> 00:32:55.658
"Make him listen."

00:32:56.362 --> 00:32:57.454
What are you thinking?

00:33:09.495 --> 00:33:11.126
Damn it, they're still here. Come on.

00:33:18.957 --> 00:33:21.137
Get off my property
before I call the cops!

00:33:21.184 --> 00:33:22.863
Mr. Pike, listen. Dad,

00:33:23.368 --> 00:33:24.389
They're just trying to help.

00:33:24.436 --> 00:33:25.493
Get in the house!

00:33:26.044 --> 00:33:27.712
Sorry. I told him the truth.

00:33:27.770 --> 00:33:29.602
We had a plan, Matt.
What happened to the plan?

00:33:30.412 --> 00:33:32.020
Look, it's twelve a.M.

00:33:32.161 --> 00:33:33.558
They are coming any minute now.

00:33:33.617 --> 00:33:36.704
You need to get your family
and go before it's too late.

00:33:36.835 --> 00:33:38.830
Oh, yeah, you mean
before the biblical swarm.

00:33:39.006 --> 00:33:41.437
What do you think really
happened to that realtor, huh?

00:33:41.578 --> 00:33:42.975
And the gas-Company guy?

00:33:43.421 --> 00:33:45.240
You don't think something
weird's going on around here?

00:33:45.360 --> 00:33:47.673
Look, I don't know who
you are, but you're crazy.

00:33:47.686 --> 00:33:50.146
You come near my boy or my family again,

00:33:50.243 --> 00:33:51.318
We're gonna have a problem.

00:33:51.363 --> 00:33:54.037
Well, I hate to be a downer, but we got
a problem right now. Dad, they're right.

00:33:54.256 --> 00:33:55.188
We're in danger.

00:33:56.150 --> 00:33:58.163
Matt, get inside now!

00:33:58.539 --> 00:33:59.583
Why won't you listen to me?!

00:33:59.673 --> 00:34:02.043
Because this is crazy!
It doesn't make any sense!

00:34:02.366 --> 00:34:02.900
Look,

00:34:03.160 --> 00:34:04.768
This land is cursed.

00:34:05.106 --> 00:34:08.510
People have died here. Are you gonna
really take that risk with your family?

00:34:08.522 --> 00:34:09.033
Wait.

00:34:11.212 --> 00:34:11.926
You hear it?

00:34:16.346 --> 00:34:17.405
What the hell?

00:34:22.011 --> 00:34:24.077
It's time to go. Larry, get your wife.

00:34:24.798 --> 00:34:25.219
Guys.

00:34:29.447 --> 00:34:30.536
Oh, my god.

00:34:32.616 --> 00:34:33.826
We'll never make it.

00:34:33.878 --> 00:34:35.854
Everybody in the house.
Everybody in the house!

00:34:36.070 --> 00:34:36.739
Let's go!

00:34:41.678 --> 00:34:43.858
Is there anyone else in the
neighborhood? No, it's just us.

00:34:44.497 --> 00:34:45.699
Honey, what's happening?

00:34:46.259 --> 00:34:47.303
What's that noise?

00:34:48.468 --> 00:34:49.437
Call 911.

00:34:50.256 --> 00:34:51.133
Joanie!

00:34:51.389 --> 00:34:52.020
Okay.

00:34:53.275 --> 00:34:54.870
I need towels.

00:34:54.982 --> 00:34:58.242
We got to lock this place up. Come on, doors,
windows, the fireplace, everything. Okay?

00:34:58.941 --> 00:34:59.954
Phones are dead.

00:35:00.035 --> 00:35:01.393
They must have chewed
through the phone lines.

00:35:07.563 --> 00:35:08.597
And the power lines.

00:35:08.838 --> 00:35:09.691
Maybe my cell.

00:35:13.004 --> 00:35:13.946
No signal.

00:35:14.513 --> 00:35:15.487
You won't get one.

00:35:16.220 --> 00:35:17.880
They're blanketing the house.

00:35:34.897 --> 00:35:35.955
So, what do we do now?

00:35:36.682 --> 00:35:37.673
We try to outlast it.

00:35:39.711 --> 00:35:42.469
Hopefully the curse will
end at sunrise. Hopefully?

00:36:05.485 --> 00:36:07.270
Bug spray? Trust me.

00:36:10.229 --> 00:36:10.776
What is that?

00:36:21.281 --> 00:36:22.161
The flue.

00:36:24.975 --> 00:36:26.748
I think everybody needs to get upstairs.

00:36:37.968 --> 00:36:40.226
Everybody upstairs now! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:36:43.607 --> 00:36:44.956
Quick!

00:36:53.763 --> 00:36:56.248
Okay, Joanie, go, go, go.

00:36:56.285 --> 00:36:57.236
Matt, go.

00:36:58.797 --> 00:36:59.888
Hurry!

00:37:06.666 --> 00:37:07.652
You in? Yeah.

00:37:10.812 --> 00:37:12.574
Come on!

00:37:19.185 --> 00:37:20.582
My god, what's that?!

00:37:26.915 --> 00:37:28.161
Something's eating through the wood.

00:37:29.587 --> 00:37:30.428
Termites.

00:37:34.870 --> 00:37:36.259
All right, everybody get back.

00:37:36.414 --> 00:37:37.856
Get back! Get back!

00:37:37.886 --> 00:37:38.456
Get back!

00:37:39.530 --> 00:37:40.318
Matt.

00:38:42.099 --> 00:38:44.492
Huddle together. Cover your faces.

00:38:55.252 --> 00:38:56.015
Look!

00:39:57.382 --> 00:39:58.328
What, no goodbye?

00:39:58.853 --> 00:39:59.694
Good timing.

00:39:59.807 --> 00:40:01.278
Another hour and we'd have been gone.

00:40:01.834 --> 00:40:02.449
For good?

00:40:03.388 --> 00:40:03.998
Yeah.

00:40:04.051 --> 00:40:07.820
The development's been put on hold while the
government investigates those bones you found,

00:40:08.255 --> 00:40:09.644
But I'm gonna make damn sure

00:40:09.774 --> 00:40:10.908
No one lives here again.

00:40:11.704 --> 00:40:13.152
You don't seem too upset about it.

00:40:14.385 --> 00:40:17.621
Well, this has been the biggest
financial disaster of my career, but,

00:40:19.047 --> 00:40:20.158
Somehow...

00:40:22.059 --> 00:40:23.366
I really don't care.

00:40:38.651 --> 00:40:39.560
What's this?

00:40:39.792 --> 00:40:40.618
I don't know.

00:40:41.827 --> 00:40:42.510
They

00:40:42.788 --> 00:40:44.109
Kind of weird me out now.

00:40:46.690 --> 00:40:48.090
Yeah, I should hope so.

00:41:09.116 --> 00:41:10.197
I want to find dad.

00:41:12.004 --> 00:41:12.807
Yeah, me too.

00:41:14.421 --> 00:41:15.525
Yeah, but I just...

00:41:18.915 --> 00:41:20.341
I want to apologize to him.

00:41:23.884 --> 00:41:24.508
For what?

00:41:27.082 --> 00:41:28.793
All the things I said to him.

00:41:31.651 --> 00:41:33.115
He was just doing the best he could.

00:41:36.483 --> 00:41:38.090
Well, don't worry, we'll find him,

00:41:39.298 --> 00:41:40.752
And you'll apologize,

00:41:41.573 --> 00:41:44.196
And within five minutes, you guys
will beat each other's throats.

00:41:48.274 --> 00:41:50.116
Yeah, probably.

00:41:52.872 --> 00:41:54.444
Let's hit the road. Let's.



